                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "426340d3-af14-3795-b393-633fcb51b6a9",
                        "entry_id": "8fe17a92-7016-340c-bdfc-ee625e47e47e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "rood tot bruinrood mineraal, kwiksulfide, HgS"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3b5512c-c38e-4a88-9bb1-36626c955e71",
                                "sense_id": "426340d3-af14-3795-b393-633fcb51b6a9",
                                "text": "„Het glas was zo kapot dat alles - zeven kisten vol - bijna zonder nader onderzoek naar ons depot was verdwenen”, vertelt archeochemicus Christian-Heinrich Wunderlich in Halle. Bijna. Maar het viel Wunderlich op dat op veel scherven metalige en rode substanties zaten. Een snelle chemische analyse maakte duidelijk dat het glaswerk onder meer kwikzilver, cinnaber, zwavelzuren, en vooral antimoon bevat moest hebben. Toen wist Wunderlich genoeg: de glasberg kon wel eens afval van een alchemistenwerkplaats geweest zijn."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6dbf267-d7f6-403d-8c1b-7acedf985a81",
                                "sense_id": "426340d3-af14-3795-b393-633fcb51b6a9",
                                "text": "Reeds in de klassieke oudheid was de slechte invloed van kwikdampen op de menselijke gezondheid goed bekend. De Romeinen stuurden dan ook gevangenen naar Spanje om in de mijnen aldaar cinnaber (kwiksulfide) te winnen dat met zijn prachtige vermiljoenrode kleur een begeerde delfstof voor gebruik bij de verfbereiding was."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8c30de09-4e99-444f-95d6-a34514f8ba4a",
                        "source_entry_id": "8fe17a92-7016-340c-bdfc-ee625e47e47e",
                        "source_sense_id": "426340d3-af14-3795-b393-633fcb51b6a9",
                        "target_lang_word": "vermilion",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "vermilion",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "50622a33-6130-3c05-948a-ebb92735acda",
                                        "entry_id": "68da5f33-4073-3cc4-b5d1-0bc709f60398",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A vivid red synthetic pigment made of mercury sulfide, cinnabar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "524d9b2c-2be8-44b0-882b-58288d062391",
                                                "sense_id": "50622a33-6130-3c05-948a-ebb92735acda",
                                                "text": "Take ſix Ounces of Brimſtone, and melt it in an Iron Ladle, then put two Pound of Quick-ſilver into a ſhammy Leather, or double Linnen Cloth, and ſqueeze it out into the melted Brimſtone, ſtirring them, in the mean Time, with a wooden Spatula till they are well united; and when they are cold, beat the Maſs into a Powder, and ſublime it in a Glaſs-veſſel, with a ſtrong Fire, and it will riſe into that Red Subſtance, which is called artificial Cinnabar or Vermilion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "727a56bd-1e71-4fa2-8839-3bb483ae8856",
                                                "sense_id": "50622a33-6130-3c05-948a-ebb92735acda",
                                                "text": "Fanny was very pretty; her eyes were dark and brilliant, her teeth were like little pearls; her mouth was almost as red as Mademoiselle Caracoline’s when the latter had put on her vermilion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "49051a98-e143-39ff-aa52-42667be3e0ac",
                                        "entry_id": "68da5f33-4073-3cc4-b5d1-0bc709f60398",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bright orange-red colour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f22970ef-7dff-410a-a597-b7ece40ed9be",
                                                "sense_id": "49051a98-e143-39ff-aa52-42667be3e0ac",
                                                "text": "While this particular difference in the shade of vermilion is very striking in the symmetrical, smooth skins of even and regular make, which I have just compared, I must confess that it probably would not be in rough skins such as some European ornithologists appear still content with."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8d02355e-995f-304d-a850-caddd9aa7700",
                                        "entry_id": "68da5f33-4073-3cc4-b5d1-0bc709f60398",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of red dye worn in the parting of the hair by married Hindu women."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "47bc3100-2b3c-38f4-ae55-780fb156f950",
                                        "entry_id": "68da5f33-4073-3cc4-b5d1-0bc709f60398",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The red skin of the lips or its border with the skin of the face."
                                        ],
